    "body": "@davidkna I am using nvm. I tried switching over to `fnm` and am seeing a similar result. \r\n\r\nAfter further investigation, this may not be an issue with starship at all. I cloned the repo and ran the same command on another machine. This time I got a much lower time.\r\n\r\n```\r\n Here are the timings of modules in your prompt (>=1ms or output):\r\n nodejs      -  13ms  -   \"via  v16.17.0 \"\r\n git_status  -   11ms  -   \"[?] \"\r\n directory   -    <1ms  -   \"ng-bc/cards \"\r\n git_branch  -   <1ms  -   \"on  main \"\r\n line_break  -   <1ms  -   \"\\n\"\r\n character   -   <1ms  -   \"❯ \"\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe first test was on my work machine, an M1 Max, and this new one is my personal machine, an M1 Pro. The dotfiles are the same between both machines. \r\n\r\nI am closing this issue because I assume the slowdown is being caused by some management software on my work machine. \r\n",
